  <h2 id="sales">Who pays for these skills, and how they judge you</h2>

  <p>
    Employers pay for people who can show they have done a version of the work. They judge you by bridge projects, references and clear stories.
  </p>
  <p>
    The first basic skill is telling your switch story in two sentences.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">AI and MBA to switch careers: which tasks are under pressure</h2>

  <p>
    AI tools draft applications and analyses. Routine drafting shrinks.
  </p>
  <p>
    Judgment, leadership and credible proof hold value. A staged path helps: now, use AI to draft and refine; later, own the new role.
  </p>

